# Golden Signals & USE Bottleneck Analysis

## 1\. Executive Summary

The Golden Signals and USE analysis identifies **database connection pool saturation** as the primary bottleneck affecting the application.

The strongest degradation occurs on POST /api/v1/checkout and POST /api/v1/reports/export. Both endpoints consume the maximum **50/50 database connections** and have requests waiting for database connections.

POST /api/v1/checkout has a P99 latency of **6800 ms**, an error rate of **17.65%**, **98% worker\-thread utilization**, and **142 database requests waiting**.

POST /api/v1/reports/export also reaches **50/50 database connections**, has **68 waiting database requests**, and an error rate of **28.89%**.

In comparison, CPU utilization is only **41.5%**, memory utilization is **62.4%**, and network bandwidth utilization is **28.3%**. Therefore, CPU, memory, and network bandwidth are not the primary bottlenecks.

The evidence indicates that database connection pool exhaustion blocks application workers, increases request latency, generates errors, and eventually contributes to TCP listen backlog saturation.

